    <!--
        Contact.AccountId is LOAD-BEARING FOR THE IR CONVERSION, not a display grant. Step 4 of
        InvestorLeadConvertService (detachContacts) writes AccountId = null to release the investor
        Contact from the temporary Account before that Account is deleted. Until 2026-08-16 this
        grant was absent from EVERY parent held by the IR persona. Measured: a FieldPermissions
        query for Contact.AccountId returned rows for roughly 99 other permission sets but none for
        DPEG_IR_Default_Access, DPEG_App_IR, or the DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access profile, while an
        administrator (who has it via xDO_Base_Access / SDO_Admin_Base_Access) could run the same
        conversion cleanly. That asymmetry matches the reported symptom exactly: the investor
        Contact kept its temporary Account, the Account was therefore deliberately not deleted, and
        yet the step 7 fields (RecordTypeId, Is_Accredited__c) DID save. Only the statement
        touching THIS field failed.
        The requirement is that every holder of this permission set gets the identical result, so
        the field the feature writes is granted here explicitly rather than relying on the persona
        inheriting it from somewhere else.
    -->
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Contact.AccountId</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Contact.Email</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
